{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.ODE.Gronwall","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.ExpDeriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.RealDeriv","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Module","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Module.FiniteDimension"],"declarations":38,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.kzExchange_shadow_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.kzExchange_shadow_involution","kind":"theorem","line":395,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L395-L398","doc":"The shadow involution of `QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy` for the two-point KZ exchange:\nat `q = 1` the exchange squares to the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.flip_mul_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.flip_mul_flip","kind":"theorem","line":388,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L388-L393","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.kzExchange_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.kzExchange_zero","kind":"theorem","line":382,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L382-L386","doc":"**The classical shadow is the flip, an involution.** At `c = 0` (`q = 1`, no deformation)\nthe KZ exchange is the transposition of the two points: the shadow involution\n`QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_involution`, here at the specialisation `c = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.kzExchange_quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.kzExchange_quad","kind":"theorem","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L362-L380","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic, expanded, as the monodromy relation of the KZ exchange.**\n`β² = (q − q⁻¹) β + 1` with `q = e^c`. This is the form of the field\n`QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.quad`, here *derived* from the flat connection on two points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.kzExchange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.kzExchange","kind":"def","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L358-L360","doc":"The normalised KZ exchange `β = e^{c/2} · P · Hol` on `V ⊗ V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.exchange_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.exchange_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L344-L355","doc":"**The KZ exchange satisfies the Hecke quadratic** — derived from the flat connection,\nnot assumed. With `q = e^c` (`c = iπλ`), `β = e^{c/2} · P · Hol` obeys\n`(β − q)(β + q⁻¹) = 0`, equivalently `β² = (q − q⁻¹)β + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.real_q_admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.real_q_admissible","kind":"theorem","line":334,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L334-L342","doc":"At a real `q > 1` the hypothesis `q² + 1 ≠ 0` holds, so the theorem applies\nat the purely imaginary coupling `λ = ln q / (iπ)` (`c = iπλ = ln q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.trace_weight_exchange_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.trace_weight_exchange_pow","kind":"theorem","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L324-L332","doc":"**Weighted trace.** For every two-strand braid `σ^k`, the weighted trace of\nthe KZ monodromy equals that of the Jimbo R-matrix, times the writhe scalar\n`e^{-kc/2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.exchange_eq_conj_rCheck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.exchange_eq_conj_rCheck","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L318-L322","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.exchange_eq_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.exchange_eq_classical","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L297-L316","doc":"**Two-strand Drinfeld–Kohno.** The KZ exchange operator `flip · Hol` equals\n`e^{-c/2}` times the classical exchange at `q = e^{c}`, hence `e^{-c/2}` times a\nweight-preserving conjugate of the Jimbo `Ř(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.transport_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.transport_one","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L294-L295","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.halfMonodromy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.halfMonodromy","kind":"def","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L289-L292","doc":"The KZ half-monodromy matrix: transport over `[0,1]` at `c = iπλ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.kz_solution_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.kz_solution_unique","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L265-L287","doc":"**Uniqueness.** Any solution of `F' = c Ω F` on `[0,1]` with `F(0) = x`\nequals the explicit transport there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.transport_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.transport_zero","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L262-L263","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.transport_hasDerivAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.transport_hasDerivAt","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L238-L260","doc":"The transport solves the KZ system `F' = c Ω F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.casimir_mulVec_transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.casimir_mulVec_transport","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L224-L236","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.transport","kind":"def","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L218-L222","doc":"The explicit KZ transport: `F(t)x = e^{ct/2} x + (e^{-3ct/2} − e^{ct/2}) P_anti x`,\ni.e. `exp(ctΩ)` written through `Ω = ½ − 2 P_anti`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.halfTurn_logDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.halfTurn_logDeriv","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L205-L216","doc":"Along the half-turn `w(t) = w₀ e^{iπt}`, the logarithmic derivative is `iπ`,\nso `λ Ω dlog w` pulls back to `(iπλ) Ω dt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.classicalExchange_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.classicalExchange_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L184-L197","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic of the classical exchange.** `q P_sym − q⁻¹ P_anti` has the two\neigenvalues `q` and `−q⁻¹`, so `(β − q)(β + q⁻¹) = 0`. This is the relation the corpus\ncalls the \"curvature\" `F(σ) = σ² − (q − q⁻¹)σ − 1`; here it is an eigenvalue relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.trace_weight_classicalExchange_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.trace_weight_classicalExchange_pow","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L157-L182","doc":"The weighted trace of every power of the classical exchange equals that of\n`Ř(q)`, because the conjugator preserves weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.classicalExchange_eq_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.classicalExchange_eq_conj","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L152-L155","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.rCheck_mul_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.rCheck_mul_conj","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L144-L150","doc":"**Algebraic core.** `Ř(q) · S = S · (q P_sym − q⁻¹ P_anti)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.classicalExchange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.classicalExchange","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L140-L142","doc":"The classical exchange shape `q·P_sym − q⁻¹·P_anti`, written with `P_anti`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.conj_commute_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.conj_commute_weight","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L134-L138","doc":"The conjugator preserves total weight: it commutes with `K ⊗ K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.conjInv_mul_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.conjInv_mul_conj","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L127-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.conj_mul_conjInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.conj_mul_conjInv","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L120-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.qq_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.qq_ne","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L114-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.casimir_eq_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.casimir_eq_flip","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L106-L112","doc":"On `ℂ² ⊗ ℂ²` the split Casimir is the flip minus one half. This is why the\n`n`-point KZ residues are `s_{ij} − ½` in the symmetric-group algebra\n(content block `def:kz-connection-sl2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.flip_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.flip_eq","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L102-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.casimir_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.casimir_eq","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L98-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.antiProj_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.antiProj_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L93-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.conjInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.conjInv","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L86-L91","doc":"Its inverse, when `q + q⁻¹ ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.conj","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L77-L84","doc":"The weight-preserving conjugator: identity on `↑↑` and `↓↓`, and on the\nweight-zero block it sends the classical eigenvectors `↑↓ ± ↓↑` to the\n`q`-eigenvectors of `Ř`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.weightKK","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.weightKK","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L73-L75","doc":"The weight operator `K ⊗ K`, `K = diag(1, q²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.rCheck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.rCheck","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L65-L71","doc":"The Jimbo R-matrix `Ř(q)` of `U_q(𝔰𝔩₂)` on `V ⊗ V`\n(eigenvalue `q` on the triplet, `-q⁻¹` on the singlet). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.flip","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L58-L63","doc":"The flip `x ⊗ y ↦ y ⊗ x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.antiProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.antiProj","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L51-L56","doc":"The projector onto the antisymmetric (singlet) line. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.casimir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoTwoPoint.casimir","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoTwoPoint.lean#L44-L49","doc":"The split Casimir `Ω = e⊗f + f⊗e + ½ h⊗h` on `V ⊗ V`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}